            {
              "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/process/Process_L2ComponentEditReview",
              "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
              "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/l2-component-edit-review.svg",
              "description": "One pass over one L2 DAK component: the agent edits it, runs its checker, renders and stages it with a before/after, and hands it on; review forks off beside the hand-on and never holds it up (adjudication is QA, not a gate). Called once per component pass by each authoring track of l2-dak-authoring.bpmn (Process_L2Dak).\n\nOnly the call's inputs differ between components (skill l2-component-edit-review, \"The inputs, per component\"):\n- component: personas and user scenarios (C2, C3), business processes (C4), core data elements and glossary (C5) with their terminology bindings, decision-support and scheduling logic (C6, C7), indicators and requirements (C8, C9);\n- authoring skill: l2-dak-authoring, bpmn-authoring, dmn-authoring or terminology-management, named on the calling activity, so it joins this process's skills along the call path (review-task.bpmn's scoped composition);\n- renderer and diff: what the reviewer sees, before and after;\n- checker: the mechanical checks the agent runs before asking anyone;\n- reviewing role: the person who takes this process's reviewer lane for the call.",
              "enforcement": "advisory",
              "flowCount": 13,
              "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-L2",
              "name": "L2 component edit and review",
              "nodeCount": 13,
              "sourcePath": "L2/collab/processes/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn",
              "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/smart-base/blob/main/smart-base/L2/collab/processes/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn",
              "startNode": "http://smart.who.int/base/process/Process_L2ComponentEditReview/node/Start_ComponentPass",
              "summary": "One pass over one L2 DAK component: the agent edits it, runs its checker, renders and stages it with a before/after, and hands it on; review forks off beside the hand-on and never holds it up (adjudication is QA, not a gate)."
            },
